welcome back to curious archive this  video is the second part of a series  exploring the incredible speculative  evolution project of serena the world of  birds serena was created by dylan betta  an exceptional artist and worldbuilder i  have links below where you can follow  and support his work when we left off  serena was just beginning to warm at the  end of the cryoscene era  now it is the thermoscene a hothouse  world of rising sea levels and  increasing volcanic activity that has  led to some extinctions especially  within the warming oceans where large  animals like the balloons have sadly  died out in much of the world however  newly evolved species are enjoying this  new climate 100 million years into this  grand experiment birds have evolved to  fill virtually every niche this moon has  to offer in the warm forest a descendant  of the cerelips of the cryoscene ambles  through the woods their feathers have  become coats of short fuzz and their  beaks have given way to fleshy snouts  indeed these creatures look quite a bit  like the non-avian dinosaurs of old in  sides and behavior however the animals  are almost analogous to an earth deer  elsewhere in the warm forests the  cerelopes have become the more  specialized horned omnivores known as  the ornitheries the beaks of these  animals are now little more than  incisors within an almost mammalian  looking snout and in the canopy above  flightless monkey-like mucks swing from  the branches which despite their size  are actually an offshoot of the massive  cryoscene sarahstriders but the larger  sarah striders are still with us in the  thermoscene just changed since we last  saw them  serra striders are huge armored titans  that have traded in their feathers for  defensive spikes later in the therma  scene some sarah striders would  specialize further becoming heavily  armored goliaths called crag backs these  bony plates help the animals deter large  predators primarily the tyrant sarins  bone-crushing hunters who have endured  beyond the cryoscene in this age of  dinosaur-like megafauna one might be  paying little attention to the  achievements of the mud wickets which  are now called the tripits and have  become truly terrestrial fish fully  independent from the water the tributes  have spread out into the jungles with  their tails specializing into a fully  functional foot this strange tripod-like  walking strategy isn't perhaps the most  efficient just yet but evolution is  blind and the tributes are making it  work another easily overlooked group  from the later thermoscene are the  bumblets small quadrupedal burrowers at  only 7 inches in length these tiny  tunnelers don't appear destined for  greatness but times will soon change  elsewhere during the thermoscene the  waters largely empty of megafauna due to  cryoscene extinctions now represent a  unique opportunity for any species brave  enough to venture into the depths for  example gigadocks are a type of  saristriders that have become  semi-aquatic adopting the webbed feet  and lake paddling lifestyle of ducks on  earth just on a much larger scale as  weigh up to a ton since newborn  gigaducks have trouble foraging in deep  waters mother gigaducks care for their  chicks during their development often  carrying them on their back  in deeper waters you can find the  porpoints a highly varied classification  of aquatic birds these sleek swimmers  evolved later than the balloons which is  why they weren't wiped out by the  cryoscene extinctions the overall body  shape and flipper-derived fins make some  porpins resemble penguins whereas the  larger ones seem similar to a porpoise  or dolphin  in the depths of the oceans the sword  whales now flourish gigantic descendants  of cryoscene sword sharks these giants  now have larger mouths that allow them  to feed upon vast schools of plankton  and reach incredible sizes while these  sword whales are gentle giants the  gigadon a variety of sword whales are  decidedly not these orca whale-sized  predators don't just possess sharp jaws  but also unusually keen minds for fish  they use these large brains to  coordinate pack hunting aided by their  reflective markings on their skin that  they can use incredibly as a form of  basic communication elsewhere in the  depths we have the less intelligent and  far less elegant looking lump head  grumpus a creature that might have the  best name of anything on serena these  slow-moving moleskeeters have evolved  elongated fin-like structures on their  faces that help them navigate the pitch  black waters while they search for food  a very unique looking species indeed  leaving the waters the isolated crying  islands have also changed quite a bit  since our last visit the islands  themselves are smaller due to erosion  and rising sea levels and have become  more tropical in climate in the species  populating these islands have also  become far stranger instead of snuffalos  and butcher raptors you can now find  creatures like the elephants's truly  unique looking birds with two  tentacle-like appendages that can grasp  food and other objects how did something  like this possibly evolve from a bill  well elephants are descended from  burrowers whose bills became fleshier  and more flexible to aid with rooting  through the dirt for food over millions  of years these bills became softer and  more muscular eventually splitting into  two distinct trunk-like apparatuses and  so one of the strangest creatures on  serena emerged the perhaps somewhat less  impressive cousins of the elephants on  these islands are the snuffles small  soft snouted nocturnal birds with  sensitive whiskers that aid in their  nighttime hunts for food one offshoot of  this group the water snuffles has  something even stranger than whiskers  sprouting from the ends of its spill  fleshy finger-like appendages similar in  some ways to the elefinch's trunks a  really unique looking creature and in  the midst of this incredible peak of  biodiversity on the crying islands the  oceans and the mainlands the tributes  the terrestrial descendants of the mud  wicket fishes have in the late  thermoscene become strange three-legged  organisms called hoppers the adaptation  of these unique animals into land  dwellers has been a true achievement and  they're now thriving in the warm  temperatures still the hoppers are only  about the size of a rat it would take a  mass extinction for them to ever become  a dominant species on serena which is  exactly what happened next a rise in  global temperatures volcanic fumes  eruptions and ocean anoxia creates a  runaway effect that results in the worst  mass extinction event in the moon's  history simply called armageddon the end  thermosene extinction would obliterate  over 99 of all life on serena but this  cataclysm was not the end eventually  armageddon would pass and the sun would  rise on the pangaea scene it is now 10  million years after this mass extinction  and the fire and brimstone are already a  distant memory for many species in this  era all of serena's major land masses  have come together to form a single  super continent the climate has somewhat  stabilized and the survivors of  armageddon are beginning to rediversify  but the inheritors of this new world are  quite different from its old monarchs if  one explores the continental forests of  this reborn moon one would find far  stranger life than ever before  lumbering amongst the trees comes a  terrestrial muck a descendant of one of  their smaller ancestors these hook  clawed creatures might look odd but  they're far from the strangest new forms  of life here from the water comes a  descendant of the water snuffle one of  the only species from the crying islands  to survive thanks to its aquatic  adaptations the finger like tendrils on  the ends of their beaks are becoming  more pronounced and may soon become even  more complex out of a nearby riverbank  erupts a bumblet the sole survivor out  of all the vivas that for millions of  years dominated the planet it's  fascinating that out of all its grand  cousins thanks to his burrowing  lifestyle the bumblet is now the sole  representative of the great evolutionary  line and at the edge of the forest  attribute here the much-changed  descendant of the tributes and by  extension the mud wickets stalks for  prey they've become a muscular dog-like  carnivore with a powerful hind leg that  allows them to make great lunges at prey  once at the bottom of serena's food  chain their time has now finally come  over the next several million years  through the early and middle pangea  scene members of this group called the  kanethirs would prove to be the most  successful and prominent large predators  on serena the author writes that the  predator's flexible spine which moves in  an up and down arc works almost like a  spring collecting energy as the creature  contracts its leg and releasing it as it  extends making for an efficient running  gate it's hard to imagine that these  dominant warm-blooded furry organisms  were once fish brought in to be the  canaries food source another descendant  of the terrestrial fish has taken to the  trees becoming the somewhat alarming  looking hand fish these creatures look  like a cross between a monkey a frog and  a spider with long fractal line digits  well suited to climbing and holding onto  branches later in the pangaea scene  descendants from the same group would  even conquer the air with the tribats  now taking to the sky alongside the  birds the first group of vertebrates on  serena to independently develop powered  flight while their wing design isn't  quite as efficient as birds in the open  sky tribets are the most common animals  of the tropical forests but the birds  are not down for the count just yet  indeed several million years into the  pangaea scene flying birds have managed  to reach sizes never before seen in  their history these majestic giants are  called archangels the descendants of  small tree-dwelling ancestors who had  lasted the thermosene extinction and  then rapidly grew to sizes rivaling the  largest pterosaurs scampering nearby on  the open plains are herds of sarah's els  a descendant of the same avian  armageddon survivor as the archangels  though cerezels have become swift-footed  grazers they are marked with bold  contrasting patterns of stripes and  spots which likely serve to hide their  outlines when moving in large groups  just as is the case for zebra on our own  planet but the sarasel's dominance on  the plains wouldn't last in the later  pangea scene they'll be edged out by the  circu agadons a highly specialized group  of tributeers that are unrecognizable  compared to their fish ancestors the  circuagodonts possess specialized teeth  that allow them to eat a wider variety  of grasses than sarah's els allowing  them to eventually usurp the sarasota's  place on the planes indeed beyond the  pangaea scene it's not megafauna like  the sarah's els or archangels that will  contribute the most to the legacy of  birds on serena in time the humble  bumblets move above ground becoming a  group of foragers called bumble badgers  and in the game of life they're a new  player to keep an eye on also furthering  the legacy of birds though taking it in  an admittedly strange direction are the  excellently named mittens these  descendants of the water snuffle have  developed a mobile set of tentacles on  their snouts which they use to  manipulate food items the somewhat  cthulhu looking creatures are indeed  quite intelligent and are starting to  use basic tools in time the mittens  branch off into the plane's dwelling  bludge birds animals that use crude  weapons to aid in hunting these  creatures are clearly fairly intelligent  perhaps even one of the most intelligent  species ever to exist on serena however  despite appearances they're not actually  smarter than say crows or great apes  from our own world indeed to find the  first true example of high intelligence  on serena one must look elsewhere  watching the bludge birds from the  branches are fork-tailed babbling jays  unlike the bludge bird this small  species is not extraordinary for its  appearance furthermore they are a very  young species having only been in  existence for no more than 4 000 years  yet babbling jays are easily the  smartest creatures yet to arise on  serena possessing an incredible capacity  for tool crafting language and critical  thinking jays even produce art using  bark and stone and possess verbal  superstitions and a developing culture  sadly this brief glimmer of brilliance  wouldn't last in a relative blink of an  eye the harsh desert environment that  spurred the development of their keen  intellect would shift once again and the  jays would prove that no species no  matter their intelligence is immune to  extinction looking forwards beyond the  pangaea scene it is neither the babbling  jays nor the bludge birds that will  continue to carry the torch of  intelligence onwards  instead high intelligence will arise in  some of the most unexpected species part  3 of this series will cover the  emergence of true sapience on serena but  for now that's all the time we have if  you enjoyed learning about serena  consider following and supporting dylan  beta using the links below  also thanks for watching if you enjoyed  this entry please lend your support and  like subscribe and hit the notification  icon to stay up to date on all things  curious see you in the next video

